WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:05.010
Adult Swim's hit animated series Rick and
Morty is chock full of sophisticated ideas,

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.859
vulgar weirdness, and, well….

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:08.610
"High concept, sci-fi rigamarole!"

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:13.190
...which makes it one of the twistiest and
time-bendiest shows on television, fostering

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:17.950
hundreds of ideas about the show's alleged
secrets... some far stranger than others.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:22.270
Hold on to your brain buckets and try to keep
up with these seriously bizarre Rick and Morty

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.880
fan theories.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.450
Not the real Morty

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.010
Let's start off by flipping your whole world
upside down and saying that the Morty Smith

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.439
we've been watching lately isn't the Morty
we started off with.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:36.941
This notion is part of a larger Rick and Morty
"Master Theory", which postulates that Rick's

00:00:36.941 --> 00:00:41.680
original Morty got trapped inside one universe:
a tragedy seen during the opening credits

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.399
of each episode, when Morty falls over and
is almost eaten by giant frog creatures.

00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:51.010
Left to fend for himself in a world of monsters,
this Morty grows to resent Rick and orchestrates

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.710
the events seen in "Close Rick-Counters of
the Rick Kind" in order to take down all Ricks

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.100
in all universes.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.350
We see something like that happen in the season
three episode "The Ricklantis Mixup," in which

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.629
Politician Morty becomes President of the
Citadel of Ricks.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:08.840
Sick with power, President Morty assassinates
a number of members of the Shadow Council

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.490
of Ricks, and in a slow-motion sequence of
legal documents and floating corpses, it's

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.039
revealed that he's none other than Evil Morty.

00:01:16.039 --> 00:01:20.529
With how often Rick calls Morty disposable,
we may have called dozens of Morties our own

00:01:20.529 --> 00:01:21.529
by now.

00:01:21.529 --> 00:01:23.569
"Most timelines have a Rick and most Ricks
have a Morty.

00:01:23.569 --> 00:01:26.049
This place is a real who's-who of who's you
and me."

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:29.369
And honestly, is there that much difference
between one Morty and another?

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:33.709
"We both know that if there's any truth in
the universe, it's that Ricks don't care about

00:01:33.709 --> 00:01:35.060
Mortys."

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.359
Not the real Rick

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:40.820
Beyond our Morty not being true-blue, our
Rick might be an alternate version as well.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.229
One theory is that Rick ended his life when
Beth was a child, explaining why he was "missing"

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:46.669
from her life for 20 years.

00:01:46.669 --> 00:01:50.670
The Rick that viewers know now would have
been alive in a different dimension, separated

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.829
from Beth and his ex-wife.

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:56.989
Unfortunately, this Rick royally flubbed up
his timeline and needed a quick remedy.

00:01:56.989 --> 00:02:01.139
Discovering a universe in which a version
of himself was dead, our Rick jumped into

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:03.409
that timeline, and the rest is history.

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:07.280
We've even seen something like that happen
in the series, so any Rick is possible.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.830
And if this Rick's been gone for 20 years,
how can there be a picture of him holding

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.350
Baby Morty, who's only a teenager now?

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.530
And how can he actually remember holding Morty?

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.700
Plot hole, or secret hint that things are
even more messed up than we know?

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.140
The universe switch

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.070
It's time to unpack the Rick and Morty theory
known as "The Ticket Theory," which connects

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:29.830
the episodes "Mortynight Run" and "Total Rickall"
to suggest that the latter episode is happening

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:33.470
in a universe that isn't the one our usual
Rick and Morty operate in.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:37.270
According to the theory, the universe swap
happened when Rick and Morty picked Jerry

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:41.050
up from the Jerryboree.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:45.410
"Uhh, that's a Blipz &amp; Chitz ticket."

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.410
"What?!"

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.730
"Way to go, Morty."

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.730
"Eh, whatever."

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:52.470
The shocker here is that the ticket Rick and
Morty are given at the beginning of "Mortynight

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:56.440
Run" is numbered 5126, but they took home
a different Jerry.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.440
"Hang onto this.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.440
The number's your dad.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.080
If you lose it, we're not going to be able
to get him back."

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.980
The audience actually follows the original
Jerry into his new universe and leaves the

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.630
original Rick and Morty behind.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:09.780
How else would you explain the arrival of
Mr. Poopybutthole a few episodes later, who's

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:14.430
treated as though he's been there all along…
at least as far as this universe is concerned?

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.430
"Ooohweee!

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.190
Amen to that!"

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.750
One and the same

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.490
Rick and Morty share a number of similar qualities,
and even the same voice actor, but they can't

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.730
actually be the same person, can they?

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:29.010
According to one theory, they 100 percent
totally are.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.480
As Rick and Morty are walking through the
Citadel, you can spot what appears to be a

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.300
combination of the pair in the same physical
body.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.151
While he could be an odd alternate dimension
Rick-Morty, the theory suggests that he's

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:41.630
actually an older Morty and younger Rick.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:44.200
As far as the blue pants go, it's pretty simple.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.360
"Is that…"

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.360
"Me…

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:47.730
I used to wear blue pants."

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:52.360
Lastly, there might be a surprising link between
Diane Sanchez, Rick's ex-wife, and the staff

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.450
member of Anatomy Park, Annie.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.390
Both ladies look surprisingly similar.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:00.220
Annie grew close to Morty during their adventure
together, but Rick ended up shrinking her

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.870
and trapping her in a container.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:06.020
"What the hell, Rick?

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.063
What the hell, man…

00:04:07.063 --> 00:04:08.063
I liked her!"

00:04:08.063 --> 00:04:11.319
The theory hints that Morty, now as Rick,
freed Annie later in life so they could be

00:04:11.319 --> 00:04:12.680
together.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.040
Baby Cronenmorty

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:19.549
The creepy, oozy Cronenberg creature from
"Auto Assimilation" was a standout, even compared

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:23.810
to the giant praying mantises and deformed
beasts that ravaged the Earth in "Rick Potion

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:24.810
Number 9".

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:29.350
But the pint-sized monster could hold a harrowing
significance if you consider this next theory.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:33.250
The only time Rick and Morty viewers have
ever seen Rick genuinely connected to anyone

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.560
has been with baby Morty.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.200
"You're crying?

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.389
Over a Morty?"

00:04:37.389 --> 00:04:39.210
"No, I'm just allergic to dips---!"

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.129
"Ugh, pathetic."

00:04:41.129 --> 00:04:44.719
This makes it all the more heartbreaking to
speculate that the Cronenberg creature from

00:04:44.719 --> 00:04:48.249
the episode is actually a baby Morty from
a different dimension.

00:04:48.249 --> 00:04:52.289
Though the moment is passed off as Rick trying
to test his invention, this theory suggests

00:04:52.289 --> 00:04:56.759
that he obliterated the baby Cronenberg, who
he actually shows affection for, as part of

00:04:56.759 --> 00:04:57.960
a "contingency plan."

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.449
In another universe that got Cronenberged,
baby Morty became a victim of the Cronenberg

00:05:02.449 --> 00:05:05.680
plague, so Rick put him in stasis until he
could find a cure.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:10.080
Rick's final act of mercy was to euthanize
the Cronenberg Morty, as the only "cure" was

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.080
to kill it.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.879
After all, the problem got so bad that Rick
had to abandon an entire planet because he

00:05:14.879 --> 00:05:17.400
couldn't, or wouldn't, fix it.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.059
Beth's real mother

00:05:19.059 --> 00:05:22.949
Mum's the word for this theory, which argues
that Beth's mother is actually the hive-mind

00:05:22.949 --> 00:05:27.430
entity Unity, seen in the season two episode,
"Auto Assimilation."

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:32.160
What if Rick's previous fling with Unity led
to one of the entity's hosts, "an Earth-like

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.590
humanoid," getting pregnant?

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:37.669
Unity eventually left Rick—but not before
separating from the pregnant host that would

00:05:37.669 --> 00:05:39.020
become Beth's mother.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:43.370
Which makes for a really, really weird situation
to raise a child in, seeing as how Beth's

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:47.529
mother wasn't in control of her body when
she met Rick or conceived a kid with him.

00:05:47.529 --> 00:05:51.659
The theory supposes that Beth's real mother,
now in control of her own body, would force

00:05:51.659 --> 00:05:54.249
Rick to leave so she could bring up Beth by
herself.

00:05:54.249 --> 00:05:58.199
"I don't know if you can appreciate what it
means to grow up without a father…"

00:05:58.199 --> 00:06:02.139
Unity being Beth's real mother would also
explain why it was so protective of Morty

00:06:02.139 --> 00:06:04.559
and Summer when they visited its planet.

00:06:04.559 --> 00:06:08.830
Treating them to endless hamburgers and sending
in a special force team to rescue them wasn't

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.589
just because they're Rick's grandchildren;
it was out of a deeper maternal instinct to

00:06:12.589 --> 00:06:14.270
keep them out of harm's way.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:15.629
Thanks, grandma.

00:06:15.629 --> 00:06:17.039
Rick's self-awareness

00:06:17.039 --> 00:06:21.150
The idea that Rick knows he's a part of a
television show is one that has long circulated

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:25.229
throughout the Rick and Morty fan community,
but does Rick's self-awareness go deeper than

00:06:25.229 --> 00:06:27.520
simply acknowledging his two-dimensional existence?

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:31.810
Think about it: Rick understands that the
only reason he's "alive" is because of a creator:

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.689
Dan Harmon, to be exact.

00:06:33.689 --> 00:06:37.699
This notion grounds itself in the photo seen
hanging on Rick's wall, which is a drawing

00:06:37.699 --> 00:06:38.699
of Harmon.

00:06:38.699 --> 00:06:40.879
Or maybe it's just a picture of Abradolph
Linkler.

00:06:40.879 --> 00:06:44.539
But only the smartest man in the universe
would have a legit pic of God, right?

00:06:44.539 --> 00:06:46.319
That is, if he's not in total denial.

00:06:46.319 --> 00:06:48.039
"There is no god, Summer.

00:06:48.039 --> 00:06:49.809
Gotta rip that band-aid off now, you'll thank
me later."

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:54.599
The theory also explains why Rick drinks almost
constantly and easily breaks the fourth wall.

00:06:54.599 --> 00:06:55.999
"See you next week everybody!"

00:06:55.999 --> 00:06:57.129
"I don't get it."

00:06:57.129 --> 00:07:00.939
As a man of science, Rick turns to alcohol
because he's unable to reconcile with there

00:07:00.939 --> 00:07:02.319
being an actual God.

00:07:02.319 --> 00:07:06.029
He knows he's being watched and understands
that once people stop tuning in to Rick and

00:07:06.029 --> 00:07:08.770
Morty, his world is destroyed forever.

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:11.759
Keeping the series alive is the only way to
keep himself alive.

00:07:11.759 --> 00:07:14.449
"Me and Rick and Morty running around!

00:07:14.449 --> 00:07:15.990
Rick and Morty time!

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:21.379
All day long, forever, a hundred days, Rick
and Morty forever, a hundred times."

00:07:21.379 --> 00:07:22.759
There's something about Tricia

00:07:22.759 --> 00:07:27.339
To Summer Smith, her classmate Tricia Lange
is little more than her shiny brunette locks

00:07:27.339 --> 00:07:31.089
and nice body, but she may be far more mysterious
than she lets on.

00:07:31.089 --> 00:07:35.900
What if Tricia is actually a Galactic Federation
agent, just like Summer's old pal Tammy, sent

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:41.110
to dimension C-137 to spy on Rick to gain
new intel after the falling-out and betrayal

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:43.180
that took place at the end of season two?

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:48.699
"In a lot of ways, what I really am… is
a deep cover agent for the Galactic Federation

00:07:48.699 --> 00:07:50.809
and you guys are a group of wanted criminals."

00:07:50.809 --> 00:07:54.319
Knowing that they can no longer spy on the
Sanchez-Smith family by befriending those

00:07:54.319 --> 00:07:59.189
close to Rick, the Galactic Federation instructed
Tricia to spend time with Summer's boyfriend

00:07:59.189 --> 00:08:04.139
Ethan and become best friends with Morty's
crush Jessica, allowing her to gather information

00:08:04.139 --> 00:08:05.909
without seeming suspicious.

00:08:05.909 --> 00:08:10.569
The theory notes that Tricia's vulgar language
is exactly how Tammy spoke when she was working

00:08:10.569 --> 00:08:11.569
undercover.

00:08:11.569 --> 00:08:15.289
And though the theory doesn't mention this,
it might be worth noting that Tammy and Tricia

00:08:15.289 --> 00:08:18.059
are voiced by the same person.

00:08:18.059 --> 00:08:19.059
Rick's real plan

00:08:19.059 --> 00:08:24.599
Another popular Rick and Morty theory postulates
that in the season three finale, Rick intended

00:08:24.599 --> 00:08:26.639
to kill Morty, not Jerry.

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:30.699
The theory points to a particular moment in
the episode that happens just after Morty

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:35.690
steals Rick's portal gun and takes Beth, Summer,
and Jerry to a secluded cabin to hide from

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.900
Rick while he trashes the White House.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:42.160
Though Morty believed his hiding spot to be
unguessable by Rick, he ends up at the cabin's

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:44.280
doorstep, gun in hand, to greet everyone.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:47.630
Beth, worried that she's actually a clone
of herself, guesses that Rick brought the

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:48.960
gun to end her life.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.060
Rick quickly clarifies.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:52.190
"Beth you crazy bitch, you're my daughter.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.510
I brought this here to kill Jerry."

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.200
"Jesus Christ."

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.040
That was just a cover-up for his true intentions.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.650
The real threat isn't Jerry, but rather a
Morty with his own portal gun.

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:07.120
Or even worse, an evil Morty with a portal
gun, especially since Morty's been getting

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.880
smarter and smarter as the seasons progress.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:14.000
When Rick sees the family is fine, he just
shifts his anger towards Jerry.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.690
Because really, he's Jerry.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:20.980
"So take your attitude to the Men's section
of K-Mart, cuz you need to cut me some slack...sss."

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.770
Too weird for words

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:26.900
And then there are the fan theories that are
just too bizarre, or too unlikely to ever

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.520
be considered canonical.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:33.571
For example, there's the insane idea that
Rick's real ex-wife might be, get this, Miss

00:09:33.571 --> 00:09:38.350
Frizzle from the Magic Schoolbus series, based
on the idea that both fictional characters

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:41.310
explore the weirdest areas of space and the
human body.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.310
Okay.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.310
"F--- em.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:44.310
F--- those people.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.120
F--- this whole thing, Ethan."

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:50.270
And what about the idea that Rick purposely
abandoned his daughter to cause her to act

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:55.160
recklessly, get pregnant at a young age, ruin
her life, and pop out a couple of brainwave-jamming

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.160
kids?

00:09:56.160 --> 00:10:00.640
Sure, except Rick could probably just clone
or kidnap whatever kind of Morty he wanted…

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:01.720
because he's Rick.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.040
Fidget spinners?

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:07.570
In one half-baked theory, they're just this
reality's version of the Gooble Box.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:08.570
And ice cream?

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:12.130
It's basically the Rick &amp; Morty version of
the answer to every question in the universe,

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.050
because, well, they talk about it a lot.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:17.560
"Well, why don't I get Beth and we'll go out
for ice cream?"

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:21.490
"Jerry, this was the most romantic weekend
I've ever had."

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:23.690
"Thanks to Coldstone Creamery."

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:24.690
"Uh…

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:28.350
I was gonna hop over to the Gloppy Drop system
and get some ice cream."

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.500
"Fun facts about this one!

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:35.950
It's got giant telepathic spiders, 11 9/11s,
aaaaand the best ice cream in the multiverse!"

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.030
And Galactic Federation Agent Tammy?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:42.720
In one bonkers theory, she's actually Rick's
long-lost, dimension-hopping granddaughter…

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:46.650
based almost exclusively on the fact that
Tammy has a similar hair color to Jerry.

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:48.530
Whoever came up with this one, well…

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:50.940
"In reality, you're as dumb as they come."

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:51.940
Pretty dumb.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:52.970
"You know what?

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:53.970
Too bad!"

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:54.970
Thanks for watching!

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.690
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.730
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

